<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>An organization wants to add your group to JACOB</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: sans-serif; color: #1a1a1a; background: #f9f9f9; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .container { max-width: 560px; margin: 32px auto; background: #fff; border-radius: 8px; padding: 32px; }
    .logo { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; color: #2563eb; margin-bottom: 24px; }
    p { line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .token { font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px; background: #f3f4f6; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 4px; word-break: break-all; }
    .footer { margin-top: 32px; font-size: 12px; color: #6b7280; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="logo">JACOB</div>
    <p>Hi {{ displayName }},</p>
    <p>
      An organization on JACOB has requested to attach your group to its
      workspace. If you consent, the org's admins will gain leader-equivalent
      visibility into the group (membership, moderation, analytics).
    </p>
    <p>
      Forward this consent code to the org admin so they can complete the
      attachment. The code expires in 60 minutes:
    </p>
    <p class="token">{{ consentToken }}</p>
    <p>
      If you did not expect this request, you can safely ignore this email —
      no action will be taken without the code.
    </p>
    <p>— The JACOB team</p>
    <div class="footer">
      You received this email because you are a leader of group {{ gid }}.
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
